  ('What is the main purpose or value of assignment operator =?','updates program state','["reads user input as text","determines evaluation order","sends a result back from a function"]','assignment operator = is important because it updates program state.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: x = 5?','assignment operator =','["function","arithmetic expression","input()"]','The example illustrates assignment operator =.'),
  ('Which statement about assignment operator = is correct?','assigns a value to a variable','["equality comparison","reads user input as text","determines evaluation order"]','assignment operator = assigns a value to a variable.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “reads user input as text”?','input()','["print()","operator precedence","parameter"]','input() reads user input as text.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of input()?','makes programs interactive','["displays output","compares two values","repeats while a condition is true"]','input() is important because it makes programs interactive.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: name = input(''Name: '')?','input()','["parameter","operator precedence","print()"]','The example illustrates input().'),
  ('Which statement about input() is correct?','reads user input as text','["print()","displays output","compares two values"]','input() reads user input as text.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “displays output”?','print()','["int","comparison operator","return"]','print() displays output.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of print()?','communicates results to the user','["represents whole numbers","executes code conditionally","iterates over a sequence"]','print() is important because it communicates results to the user.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: print(total)?','print()','["return","comparison operator","int"]','The example illustrates print().'),
  ('Which statement about print() is correct?','displays output','["input()","represents whole numbers","executes code conditionally"]','print() displays output.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “represents whole numbers”?','int','["float","if statement","while loop"]','int represents whole numbers.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of int?','supports integer arithmetic','["represents decimal numbers","chooses between two alternatives","extracts part of a string"]','int is important because it supports integer arithmetic.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: 42?','int','["while loop","if statement","float"]','The example illustrates int.'),
  ('Which statement about int is correct?','represents whole numbers','["''42''","represents decimal numbers","chooses between two alternatives"]','int represents whole numbers.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “represents decimal numbers”?','float','["str","if/else","for loop"]','float represents decimal numbers.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of float?','supports fractional numeric values','["represents text","tests additional conditions","stores an ordered mutable collection"]','float is important because it supports fractional numeric values.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: 3.14?','float','["for loop","if/else","str"]','The example illustrates float.'),
  ('Which statement about float is correct?','represents decimal numbers','["True","represents text","tests additional conditions"]','float represents decimal numbers.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “represents text”?','str','["bool","elif","string slicing"]','str represents text.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of str?','stores sequences of characters','["represents True or False","handles runtime exceptions","stores key-value pairs"]','str is important because it stores sequences of characters.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: ''Jeddah''?','str','["string slicing","elif","bool"]','The example illustrates str.'),
  ('Which statement about str is correct?','represents text','["12","represents True or False","handles runtime exceptions"]','str represents text.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “represents True or False”?','bool','["type conversion","try/except","list"]','bool represents True or False.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of bool?','supports logical decisions','["changes a value from one type to another","groups reusable statements","executes Python instructions"]','bool is important because it supports logical decisions.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: True?','bool','["list","try/except","type conversion"]','The example illustrates bool.'),
  ('Which statement about bool is correct?','represents True or False','["''True''","changes a value from one type to another","groups reusable statements"]','bool represents True or False.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “changes a value from one type to another”?','type conversion','["arithmetic expression","function","dictionary"]','type conversion changes a value from one type to another.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of type conversion?','allows numeric calculation on text input','["combines values and operators","receives input into a function","stores a value under a name"]','type conversion is important because it allows numeric calculation on text input.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: int(''25'')?','type conversion','["dictionary","function","arithmetic expression"]','The example illustrates type conversion.'),
  ('Which statement about type conversion is correct?','changes a value from one type to another','["print(''25'')","combines values and operators","receives input into a function"]','type conversion changes a value from one type to another.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “combines values and operators”?','arithmetic expression','["operator precedence","parameter","Python interpreter"]','arithmetic expression combines values and operators.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of arithmetic expression?','computes a numeric result','["determines evaluation order","sends a result back from a function","assigns a value to a variable"]','arithmetic expression is important because it computes a numeric result.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: price * quantity?','arithmetic expression','["Python interpreter","parameter","operator precedence"]','The example illustrates arithmetic expression.'),
  ('Which statement about arithmetic expression is correct?','combines values and operators','["name = input()","determines evaluation order","sends a result back from a function"]','arithmetic expression combines values and operators.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “determines evaluation order”?','operator precedence','["comparison operator","return","variable"]','operator precedence determines evaluation order.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of operator precedence?','explains why multiplication occurs before addition','["compares two values","repeats while a condition is true","reads user input as text"]','operator precedence is important because it explains why multiplication occurs before addition.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: 2 + 3 * 4?','operator precedence','["variable","return","comparison operator"]','The example illustrates operator precedence.'),
  ('Which statement about operator precedence is correct?','determines evaluation order','["a syntax comment","compares two values","repeats while a condition is true"]','operator precedence determines evaluation order.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “compares two values”?','comparison operator','["if statement","while loop","assignment operator ="]','comparison operator compares two values.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of comparison operator?','produces a Boolean result','["executes code conditionally","iterates over a sequence","displays output"]','comparison operator is important because it produces a Boolean result.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: x >= 10?','comparison operator','["assignment operator =","while loop","if statement"]','The example illustrates comparison operator.'),
  ('Which statement about comparison operator is correct?','compares two values','["x = 10","executes code conditionally","iterates over a sequence"]','comparison operator compares two values.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “executes code conditionally”?','if statement','["if/else","for loop","input()"]','if statement executes code conditionally.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of if statement?','implements one-way decisions','["chooses between two alternatives","extracts part of a string","represents whole numbers"]','if statement is important because it implements one-way decisions.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: if score >= 60:?','if statement','["input()","for loop","if/else"]','The example illustrates if statement.'),
  ('Which statement about if statement is correct?','executes code conditionally','["for x in data:","chooses between two alternatives","extracts part of a string"]','if statement executes code conditionally.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “chooses between two alternatives”?','if/else','["elif","string slicing","print()"]','if/else chooses between two alternatives.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of if/else?','handles mutually exclusive outcomes','["tests additional conditions","stores an ordered mutable collection","represents decimal numbers"]','if/else is important because it handles mutually exclusive outcomes.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: pass versus fail?','if/else','["print()","string slicing","elif"]','The example illustrates if/else.'),
  ('Which statement about if/else is correct?','chooses between two alternatives','["list traversal","tests additional conditions","stores an ordered mutable collection"]','if/else chooses between two alternatives.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “tests additional conditions”?','elif','["try/except","list","int"]','elif tests additional conditions.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of elif?','supports multi-way decisions','["handles runtime exceptions","stores key-value pairs","represents text"]','elif is important because it supports multi-way decisions.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: grade bands A/B/C?','elif','["int","list","try/except"]','The example illustrates elif.'),
  ('Which statement about elif is correct?','tests additional conditions','["function return","handles runtime exceptions","stores key-value pairs"]','elif tests additional conditions.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “handles runtime exceptions”?','try/except','["function","dictionary","float"]','try/except handles runtime exceptions.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of try/except?','prevents expected errors from crashing a program','["groups reusable statements","executes Python instructions","represents True or False"]','try/except is important because it prevents expected errors from crashing a program.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: invalid numeric input?','try/except','["float","dictionary","function"]','The example illustrates try/except.'),
  ('Which statement about try/except is correct?','handles runtime exceptions','["CSS styling","groups reusable statements","executes Python instructions"]','try/except handles runtime exceptions.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “groups reusable statements”?','function','["parameter","Python interpreter","str"]','function groups reusable statements.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of function?','reduces repeated logic','["receives input into a function","stores a value under a name","changes a value from one type to another"]','function is important because it reduces repeated logic.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: def calculate_total():?','function','["str","Python interpreter","parameter"]','The example illustrates function.'),
  ('Which statement about function is correct?','groups reusable statements','["while loop only","receives input into a function","stores a value under a name"]','function groups reusable statements.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “receives input into a function”?','parameter','["return","variable","bool"]','parameter receives input into a function.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of parameter?','makes functions reusable with different values','["sends a result back from a function","assigns a value to a variable","combines values and operators"]','parameter is important because it makes functions reusable with different values.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: def tax(amount):?','parameter','["bool","variable","return"]','The example illustrates parameter.'),
  ('Which statement about parameter is correct?','receives input into a function','["global output","sends a result back from a function","assigns a value to a variable"]','parameter receives input into a function.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “sends a result back from a function”?','return','["while loop","assignment operator =","type conversion"]','return sends a result back from a function.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of return?','lets callers use a computed value','["repeats while a condition is true","reads user input as text","determines evaluation order"]','return is important because it lets callers use a computed value.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: return total?','return','["type conversion","assignment operator =","while loop"]','The example illustrates return.'),
  ('Which statement about return is correct?','sends a result back from a function','["print only","repeats while a condition is true","reads user input as text"]','return sends a result back from a function.'),
  ('Which concept is best described as: “repeats while a condition is true”?','while loop','["for loop","input()","arithmetic expression"]','while loop repeats while a condition is true.'),
  ('What is the main purpose or value of while loop?','fits condition-controlled repetition','["iterates over a sequence","displays output","compares two values"]','while loop is important because it fits condition-controlled repetition.'),
  ('Which course concept is illustrated by this example: while balance > 0:?','while loop','["arithmetic expression","input()","for loop"]','The example illustrates while loop.'),
  ('Which statement about while loop is correct?','repeats while a condition is true','["single if","iterates over a sequence","displays output"]','while loop repeats while a condition is true.'),
